        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): load bootstrap files from agentDir alongside workspace",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nPer-agent `agentDir` bootstrap files (`SOUL.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `TOOLS.md`, etc.) were silently ignored when `agentDir` differed from `workspaceDir`. Loads bootstrap files from `agentDir` when explicitly configured, with agentDir files overriding workspace files of the same name. Filters `agentDir`-root `BOOTSTRAP.md` after setup completion, matching workspace behavior.\n\n## Linked context\n\nCloses #29387\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: AgentDir bootstrap files silently ignored — zero enforcement of per-agent access-control rules\n- Real environment tested: Local gateway with agent config specifying explicit `agentDir`\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n```\nvitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-core.config.ts src/agents/bootstrap-files.test.ts\n```\n- Evidence after fix: 1 test file, 37 tests passed (vitest 4.1.8)\n- Observed result after fix: AgentDir AGENTS.md loads and overrides workspace AGENTS.md for configured agent\n- What was not tested: Multi-agent concurrent bootstrap loading with different agentDir values\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: Single-agent unit test scope\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Commands: `vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents-core.config.ts`\n- Regression coverage: bootstrap-files.test.ts (37 tests) covers workspace-only, agentDir-only, and override scenarios\n- Before: Agent with `agentDir: \"/data/agent1\"` and `agentDir/AGENTS.md` had zero enforcement\n- After: AgentDir AGENTS.md loads and overrides workspace AGENTS.md\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- Did user-visible behavior change? Yes — agentDir bootstrap files now load and can override workspace files\n- Did config, environment, or migration behavior change? No (explicit config required; no silent default state dirs)\n- Did security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? Yes — new bootstrap source can affect agent behavior\n- What is the highest-risk area? Session state and security boundary: new file source changes agent instructions\n- How is that risk mitigated? Only applies when `agentDir` is explicitly configured; no silent default state directory overrides\n\n## Current review state\n\n- Next action: @clawsweeper re-review\n- Waiting on: ClawSweeper proof evaluation",
